Two stale expectations, both from intended code changes; the behavioural checks are unchanged.

1) Line 36 counts `this.muted || this.sfxMuted || this.reasons.size > 0` in audio/GameAudio.ts and
   expected 2 (play, playCheer). 0005d7a (GGbot, Exit B5.5 audio) intentionally added a third gate in
   the exit-cine playback path (skips sfx_exit_outbound when muted/suspended, marks 'skipped-muted'),
   so it failed "3 !== 2" although every SFX path honours sfxMuted. Verified at f3d3614/7c1047b: 3
   matches (play, exit cine, playCheer); the two original gates are unchanged. Count 2 -> 3, message
   names the three gates.

2) Line 112 (journey book summary) pinned CHAPTERS ids to ['tide','meadow','sky']. ad17dfe (Voice
   Bot, lakeside L3) intentionally added the 4th chapter 风铃湖畔 (id 'lake', opens after mainline 12).
   This was hidden behind the Node 20 stop at line 38 and surfaced only with a TypeScript stand-in for
   stripTypeScriptTypes. Expectation -> ['tide','meadow','sky','lake']; the tide/meadow/sky summary
   assertions that follow are unchanged.

With a scratch TypeScript stand-in for node:module.stripTypeScriptTypes (not committed) all 13 checks
pass on Node 20. Without it the test needs Node >= 22.6 (handled in the next commit).
---
 tools/board-ui/test_board_ui_pure.cjs | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/board-ui/test_board_ui_pure.cjs b/tools/board-ui/test_board_ui_pure.cjs
index 253d108..2cfd1b9 100644
--- a/tools/board-ui/test_board_ui_pure.cjs
+++ b/tools/board-ui/test_board_ui_pure.cjs
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@ ok('UI flags live in localStorage under qfl.ui.* (seenTools JSON list, cabinHint
 });
 ok('GameAudio sfxMuted: qfl.audio.sfxMuted persists, mutes every SFX (UI clicks included) but not music; restored on next load', () => {
   const src = read('audio/GameAudio.ts'); assert(src.includes("const SFX_MUTE_KEY = 'qfl.audio.sfxMuted'"));
-  assert.equal((src.match(/this\.muted \|\| this\.sfxMuted \|\| this\.reasons\.size > 0/g) || []).length, 2, 'both SFX gates check sfxMuted');
+  assert.equal((src.match(/this\.muted \|\| this\.sfxMuted \|\| this\.reasons\.size > 0/g) || []).length, 3, 'all three SFX gates (play, playCheer, exit cine) check sfxMuted');
   const plain = src.replace(/^import .* from 'cc';\n/m, '').replace(/^@ccclass\('GameAudio'\)\n/m, '').replace(/export /g, '');
   const code = stripTypeScriptTypes(plain, { mode: 'transform' }) + '\nglobalThis.AudioClass = GameAudio;';
   const make = data => {
@@ -109,7 +109,7 @@ ok('cabin hint curve: 0.4 s in to 0.25, 3 × (0.7 s up to 1, 0.9 s down to 0.25)
 });
 ok('journey book summary: mainline stars per chapter x/12, challenge lock until the same chapter milestone 04/08/12 is cleared, challenge marks x/4', () => {
   const { chapterSummary, CHAPTERS } = H.load('ui/IslandPanels');
-  assert.deepEqual(CHAPTERS.map(c => c.id), ['tide', 'meadow', 'sky']); assert.equal(CHAPTERS[0].description, '听潮声，捡起海浪送来的贝壳。');
+  assert.deepEqual(CHAPTERS.map(c => c.id), ['tide', 'meadow', 'sky', 'lake']); assert.equal(CHAPTERS[0].description, '听潮声，捡起海浪送来的贝壳。');
   const journey = { unlocked: 5, records: Array.from({ length: 12 }, (_, i) => ({ bestStars: i < 4 ? 3 : i === 4 ? 2 : 0 })) };
   const a = chapterSummary(journey, { tide: 3 }, 0), b = chapterSummary(journey, null, 1), c = chapterSummary(journey, {}, 2);
   assert.equal(a.stars, 12); assert.equal(a.locked, false); assert.equal(a.challenges, 3); assert.equal(b.stars, 2); assert.equal(b.locked, true, 'mainline 05 open is not mainline 08 completed'); assert.equal(b.challenges, 0); assert.equal(c.locked, true);
